# 1. Ignore EVERYTHING in this folder
*

# 2. Allow the core engine files (The "Whitelist")
!CHANGELOG.md
!CLAUDE.md
!check.sh
!config.py
!run_master.py
!run_phase*.py
!.gitattributes
!tts_reader.py
!image_media.py
!pairings.py

# 2b. Allow the NotebookLM MASTER template (source). FILLED is generated per
# run and stays ignored; pairings_generated.json is a regenerable cache.
!NotebookLM_Prompt_BETA.txt

# 2c. Allow Scout handoff briefs. These are the durable record of a forensics
# phase — the investigation that produced a graft. CHANGELOG.md records the
# surgery; nothing else records the reasoning that justified it, and these
# briefs are written once and read months later by a session with no context.
!SCOUT_*.md

# 2d. Allow skill/architecture specs. Same reasoning as 2c: these are design
# documents read months later by a session with no context, and they are the
# only record of WHY a skill works the way it does.
!SKILL_SPEC_*.md
!MEDIC_TICKETS.md

# 2e. Allow the /medic annotation archive. Step 8 archives Medic_Notes verbatim
# HERE and only then clears the field, so this file is the sole surviving copy of
# the Chief Architect's review annotations — the QA evidence trail. Untracked, it
# was one `rm` from unrecoverable.

# 2f. Allow the feedback ledger — every sentence of the Chief Architect's in-card
# annotations with a per-sentence disposition. This is the completeness check that
# nine text-verification passes could not perform, because its unit is their words
# rather than my reading of them.

# 2g. Allow the /shorts notebook registry — maps topic -> Google account -> NotebookLM
# notebook UUID, keyed on EMAIL because the authuser index silently renumbers when an
# account is added. Untracked, a clean checkout loses the only map of where every
# video lives, and /shorts cannot tell which account it is standing in.

# 2h. Allow the sweep record — a human-readable log of what past /sweep passes found
# and whether each came back DIRTY or CLEAN. It is NOT the boundary source: /sweep
# reads the session transcript directly and does not read this file. Tracked because
# it is the only place the open-items trail across passes is written down.
!SWEEP_LOG.md

# 2i. Allow the /shorts rollback file. shorts.md §8 writes each note's previous Extra
# HERE *before* overwriting it, because AnkiConnect has NO undo — this is the sole
# record of what a card looked like before a video link was prepended. Untracked, the
# safety net that every write is taken on the strength of does not survive the folder.

# 3. Allow the Prompts folder and everything inside it
!Prompts/
!Prompts/*

# 4. Allow workflow skill files — .claude/commands/ holds all 9 phase skills
# (scout / design / redteam / surgeon / commit / compass / telemetry / medic / shorts) which ARE workflow source.
# (.claude/ itself must be un-ignored first so git can descend into it; other .claude/ contents stay ignored.)
!.claude/
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/commands/*

# 4b. Allow the preflight hook payload. .claude/settings.local.json fires this on
# every UserPromptSubmit; it is user-authored workflow source, not Claude Code
# internal data, and it is the enforcement mechanism for everything else — losing
# it silently disables the per-turn protocol check with no visible symptom.
!.claude/preflight_check.txt

# 5. Don't ignore this file itself
!.gitignore

# 6. PUBLIC SNAPSHOT ONLY — the files that make this repository readable and
# runnable by someone who is not me. Rule 1 above ignores everything not named
# here, so without these lines the published repo would have no README, no
# dependency list, and none of the placeholder inputs.
# run_backup.py is engine code: run_master.py imports it.
!README.md
!requirements.txt
!run_backup.py
!api_keys.example.py
!raw_chat.example.txt
